6. Effects of pressure on properties of noble gases and binary mixtures
The correlations developed in the previous sections are used to evaluate the effects of pressure (or density) on the thermodynamic and transport properties of the pure noble
gases and binary mixtures. The obtained results are for 2.0 MPa and 7 MPa, the typical operating pressures in space nuclear reactor power systems and terrestrial nuclear power plants with CBC engines, respectively. The present results at these pressures are at the lowest and highest temperatures in the cycle, the compressor exit of 400 K and the turbine inlet of 1200 K.
